gamescope: run on a Vulkan device that names no DRM node (Venus over vtest)

On a Mali phone the runtime's Vulkan is Mesa's Venus over a vtest socket to a server on the
device's own driver. Venus reports VK_EXT_physical_device_drm with no primary and no render node,
has no VK_KHR_external_semaphore_fd (vtest has no external sync), and can neither import dma-bufs
nor export them except through the server's host-visible (gralloc) allocations. With no node:

- createDevice runs as if the extension were absent instead of failing on the primary node;
- VK_KHR_external_semaphore_fd is optional and the Wayland backend offers no explicit sync
  (DRM syncobj timelines need a render node);
- flippable images skip the host's DRM_FORMAT_MOD_INVALID entry, and with no exportable modifier
  fall back to a plain LINEAR image exported as DRM_FORMAT_MOD_LINEAR instead of asserting;
- exportable images prefer a host-visible memory type, the one the server shares as gralloc;
- wl_shm textures are composited rather than flipped, and copied again at every commit (the
  per-wlr_buffer memo kept showing the first copy of a redrawn wl_buffer).

A device with a DRM node (Turnip on Adreno) takes none of these paths.

